Make toggling -~ in less change the rows past the end.
The - command flipped FLAG_TILDE, but the marker for rows after the end
of the input is chosen once at startup, so "-~" changed nothing that
could be seen. Choose the marker again when the flag is toggled, and
refill the screen, since the rows in buffer[] still point at the old
marker and -N tells marker rows from text rows by that pointer.

---
 miscutils/less.c |    3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/miscutils/less.c
+++ b/miscutils/less.c
@@ -1734,6 +1734,9 @@
 		break;
 	case '~':
 		option_mask32 ^= FLAG_TILDE;
+		empty_line_marker = (option_mask32 & FLAG_TILDE) ? "" : "~";
+		/* refill: buffer[] holds the old marker */
+		buffer_fill_and_print();
 		break;
 #if ENABLE_FEATURE_LESS_TRUNCATE
 	case 'S':
